course: dictionary
lesson: 10402
title: One word, many tricks
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Trick is a good example. Sometimes a trick fools someone, sometimes it shows skill, and sometimes it is a clever way of doing something. The words around it are the clues.
explain: Ask yourself what the word is doing in the sentence. Is someone being fooled? Is someone showing skill? Is someone sharing a clever method? «Animation is a lovely trick on your brain» means something that fools your brain, not a card trick you can see with your hands.
explain: Trick can also be a verb, a doing word. To trick someone is to make them believe something false. Check any meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right one.
fact: Trick can be a noun (a trick, tricks) or a verb (to trick, tricking, tricked).
fact: «Trick» can mean something done to fool or cheat someone.
fact: «Trick» can also mean a clever or funny action that needs skill, like a magic trick or a skateboard trick.
fact: «Trick» can mean a clever way of doing something, such as a trick for remembering.
fact: Phrases: play a trick on someone means to play a joke on them, and a trick question has a catch.
exercise: «Animation is a lovely trick on your brain: lots of still pictures are shown so fast that your eyes and brain blend them into movement.» What does trick mean here? | A small bit of magic in a cupboard | A joke that makes you laugh out loud | A quick game with a ball | *A clever way that fools your brain into seeing movement
exercise: «Laugh at the advert's trick, not at the person who believed it.» What does trick mean here? | A clever tip for remembering spellings | A funny song | A skill shown on a skateboard | *Something done to fool people
exercise: «Other reef animals win by tricks: a fake eye near the tail.» Find and copy the one word that means something false, made to fool. | *fake | reef | tail | animals
test: What does play a trick on someone mean? | To cheat at a board game | To win a race against someone | To teach someone a new game | *To play a joke on someone
test: Which sentence uses trick as a verb, a doing word? | The magic trick worked perfectly | *Tricky people try to trick children | Tricks are fun to learn | A trick for remembering spellings
exam: The sentence «Laugh at the advert's trick, not at the person who believed it» tells you what about the trick? | It was a skill, like swimming | It was a clever magic show | It was a funny song | *It made someone believe something false
